In  [LINK: (association football) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Association_football] , the  [LINK: (Confederation of African Football) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Confederation_of_African_Football]  (CAF) fines the  [LINK: (Senegal Football Federation) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Senegal_Football_Federation]  US$615,000 for  [LINK: (unsportsmanlike conduct) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unsportsmanlike_conduct]  during  [LINK: (the final match) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_Africa_Cup_of_Nations_final]  against  [LINK: (Morocco) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morocco_national_football_team] , fines  [LINK: (Senegalese) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Senegal_national_football_team]  coach  [LINK: (Pape Thiaw) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pape_Thiaw]  $100,000, and bans him for five  [LINK: (2027 AFCON qualifying matches) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2027_Africa_Cup_of_Nations_qualification] .  [LINK: (Senegalese) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Senegal]  players  [LINK: (Iliman Ndiaye) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iliman_Ndiaye]  and  [LINK: (Ismaila Sarr) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ismaila_Sarr]  are also banned from the first two qualifier matches. (DW)
The CAF also fines the  [LINK: (Royal Moroccan Football Federation) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Moroccan_Football_Federation]  $315,000 for unsportsmanlike conduct and interfering with  [LINK: (referees) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Referee_(association_football)] .  [LINK: (Moroccan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morocco]  captain  [LINK: (Achraf Hakimi) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Achraf_Hakimi]  is banned for two games and player  [LINK: (Ismael Saibari) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ismael_Saibari]  is banned for three. (DW)

